  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🌆 Synthwave Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Neon, night drives and VHS: names from an 80s that never quite happened."
    },
    "intro": "Good synthwave names sound like the end credits of an 80s action film: a hero with a chrome surname, a year in the name, a coastline at midnight. This **synthwave name generator** covers retrowave and outrun artists, bands and albums, with a vaporwave style for ｆｕｌｌｗｉｄｔｈ text, fake corporations and empty shopping malls.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good synthwave names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator, synthwave and vaporwave:</p><ul><li><strong>Moonracer 1983</strong>: a year in the name, a synthwave habit since the 2000s.</li><li><strong>Nightglider</strong>: one compound word that sounds like a car in a video game.</li><li><strong>Danny Danger &amp; the Datakids</strong>: a frontman with an action-hero name and a backing band.</li><li><strong>VCR-88</strong>: letters and a number, like old hardware.</li><li><strong>Rooftop Chase</strong>: an album title that's a scene from a film that was never made.</li><li><strong>Glow Sticks &amp; Gasoline</strong>: neon and petrol, the two smells of the genre.</li><li><strong>ＶＩＲＴＵＡＬ</strong>: fullwidth capitals, the signature look of vaporwave.</li><li><strong>Welcome to the Skyline Hotel</strong>: a vaporwave album that sounds like a lobby in 1995.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How synthwave and vaporwave name themselves",
        "content": "<p>Synthwave took off in the mid-2000s, made by producers who grew up on 80s film soundtracks, arcade games and the synths of John Carpenter and Vangelis. Kavinsky's \"Nightcall\", used in the film <em>Drive</em> (2011), brought it to a much wider audience. Outrun, one of its other names, comes from Sega's 1986 arcade driving game <em>Out Run</em>.</p><ul><li><strong>Years and numbers.</strong> Many acts put a year from the 80s in their name, as Timecop1983 and FM-84 do. The generator does the same: <em>Laguna Nights 1987</em>, <em>VGA-84</em>.</li><li><strong>Film heroes.</strong> A made-up action star with a band behind him: <em>Rex Racer &amp; the Night Pilots</em>.</li><li><strong>Album titles</strong> are places and moments: a motel pool, a highway, the skyline at 3am.</li></ul><p>Vaporwave came a little later, in the early 2010s. Macintosh Plus's <em>Floral Shoppe</em> (2011) is the album most people point to. It loops slowed-down muzak and adverts, and its names look like corporate logos, Japanese shop signs or text typed in wide, spaced-out letters. Choose <strong>Vaporwave</strong> for names like <em>パラダイス Multimedia</em> or <em>ＯＰＥＮ　２４　ＨＯＵＲＳ</em>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using a synthwave name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Think about the artwork.</strong> Sunsets, grids and chrome lettering are part of the genre, and a name that suggests a picture makes the cover easier.</li><li><strong>Vaporwave text is hard to search.</strong> Fullwidth letters and Japanese characters look great but people can't easily type them, so add a plain-text version in your profile.</li><li><strong>Check the name is free</strong> on Bandcamp, Spotify and YouTube before you print the first cassette.</li></ul><p>For something slower and dustier, try the <a href=\"lofi-name-generator.html\">Lo-Fi Name Generator</a>. If you want stars and space instead of neon, cosmic synth sits with the <a href=\"dungeon-synth-name-generator.html\">Dungeon Synth Name Generator</a>. For albums in any genre, the <a href=\"album-name-generator.html\">Album Name Generator</a> has more.</p><p>For more genres, see all the <a href=\"../categories/music_genres-names.html\">music genre name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good synthwave artist names?",
        "answer": "Names that sound like an 80s film or game: a compound like Nightglider, a year added to a name like Moonracer 1983, or an action hero with a band, like Danny Danger & the Datakids."
      },
